
			PhoenixMUD Policies

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Preamble:  Since we have had so many problems with people who think
    that they do not have to follow the rules just because their
    specific situation is not laid out here, this preamble will serve
    as a warning.   These policies are, in most cases, very generic.
    Just because you do not see your exact situation here does not
    mean that it is not against the rules.   If you *think* something
    may be against the rules, it probably is.  

    We have tried in the past not to have an overly fascist rules 
    policy but that has been abused by a select few.   These rules are 
    set out here to help keep the game fair and fun for all involved.  
    People who break the rules, whether written or not, WILL BE DEALT 
    WITH HARSHLY.  This may include, but is not limited to, purging, 
    slaying, taking equipment, freezing, deleting, and site banning.
    The god responding to the incident has the power to mete out
    punishment in a limited manner, full punishment will come from a
    H-Imp.  Whining and complaining will NOT help your situation. 

    On to the current rules, as they have been set forth...  

1.  You may NOT PLAYER KILL in any way, shape, or form.  Using charmed
    or aggresive mobs to somehow attack or kill another player will be
    treated as player killing and will be dealth with harshly.  This can
    be punished with freezer time all the way up to and including deletion.
    It is illegal and will not be tolerated for any reason.

2.  You may NOT PLAYER STEAL in any way, shape, or form. If you do so
    You will be hunted down and killed and your equipment given away to
    other players for their enjoyment. This includes looting other 
    player's corpses AND STEALING KILLS FROM OTHER PLAYERS--if a player 
    is in a room with a mob you may safely assume he intends to attack 
    said mob and may not attack it yourself without asking permission.  
    This does not apply if a player is idling in the room and will not
    reply to your requests--the mob will then be fair game.

3.  Please refrain from cursing (using foul language) on the public
    channels such as gossip, shout, and yell. It demeans you, offends 
    people, and makes the mud look bad. If this behavior continues you 
    WILL be fined, may lose the ability to use these channels, or in
    extreme circumstances be deleted from the mud.   This rule has
    been extended to include conversations which others may find
    racist, sexist, or otherwise harassing.   Also, be sure to use
    the proper channels for your communications.  You WILL be fined
    for consistently using the wrong channels.  

4.  Harassment of other players IN ANY FORM is not allowed.  This
    includes even *looking* at them if they ask you not to.  Harassers,
    whether mortal or immortal, will be deleted if they continue their 
    actions after a first warning.  If you are being harassed report 
    it to an implementor who will warn the harasser.  This is an
    extremely serious situation and will NOT be taken lightly.  
    PhoenixMUD is a mud for mature players.  If you cannot handle
    the responsibility of being mature you WILL be forced to leave.

5.  You are NOT permitted to create new characters for any reason other
    than to play them.  Creating multiple characters while below level
    20 is frowned upon, but not against the rules.  If you create 
    multiple characters with no use you will be prevented from doing 
    so in the future.

6.  Multi-playing is allowed BUT there is a limit of 2 characters on at
    one time per person. If you have more than 2 on at a time one of the 
    characters will be purged at random until you reach the 2 character 
    limit.  If you are in a situation where you have multiple people
    sharing a connection where all traffic appears to come from one
    site (i.e. a proxy server like Wingate) it would be a wise idea to
    let a god know so you will not be accidentally purged.

6.1 The 2 character limit does not allow you to log in 2 characters,
    drop link on one, and then bring in a third.  You will be purged
    and possibly deleted if caught doing this.

7.  You may not give away a character to another person nor may you
    accept such a character.  Any character found to be used by persons
    other than the creator will be purged and deleted.  

7.1 You may not share characters among different players.  Your character
    is your own.  Shared characters will be purged and deleted upon
    discovery.  You are responsible for any and all actions done with your
    character, whether or not it is really you using them.  For those 
    who can't take the hint--KEEP YOUR PASSWORDS SECURE AND SECRET!

8.  Camping/Hoarding.  Each character is allowed to carry 100 pieces of
    equipment on his or her person and store 25 pieces of equipment
    per room in his or her house.  Abusing bugs to camp with more than
    100 items will be dealt with very harshly, this includes dropping link.
    Obviously this does not apply to coming back into the game immediately
    after a crash.  If you think you have a poor connection and may lose
    link and not be able to reconnect, DONT CARRY MORE THAN 100 ITEMS.

8.1 Storage characters for gold, eq, gating, or any other reason
    are not permitted.  Any obvious storage character which is
    discovered by an immortal will be deleted immediately.

9.  Reimbursments for gold, eq, or levels will NOT be given out for 
    most "normal" reasons (junking your corpse, loss of corpse, 
    mobs looting your corpse, etc.)  Reimbs MAY be given for serious 
    problems like implementor error or code bugs.  NO reimbursements
    will be made if players are whiny and demand them.

10. All character names must adhere to the name policy. If a god 
    feels your name is inappropriate you will have to change it.  
    A god will not ask you to change your name after level 1 without 
    making reasonable ammends to get you back to your previous level.

11. Active advertising of other muds either in search of players or 
    immortals is absolutely prohibited and punishable by immediate
    deletion.

12. What the Gods decide in any matter is final and is not subject
    to negotiation.  You may not appeal a god's decision to any other
    god than an H-Imp.  Should you choose to appeal you must tell
    the H-Imp of the original god's decision.  Failure to do so 
    may result in deletion.  Asking any other immortal or god to do 
    something a higher or equal level immortal has already said no to 
    WILL result in deletion.  For those who don't understand:  Do not
    ask dad for something when mom has already said no and dad does
    not know that.

13. Creating a character for another player who cannot create because
    of a banned site is grounds for deletion of all of the creator's
    characters. Sites are banned for a reason--which is generally to
    prevent the creation of new characters.  Even if a player is allowed
    one character, that doesn't mean that he or she is allowed additional
    characters.  All such requests must be made through an Implementor. 

14. All players are obligated to report any bugs or anything that
    seems "funny" or out-of-sorts.  This includes anything that allows
    players to get extra gold or equipment or experience in addition
    to that normally available.  Anyone found exploiting bugs will
    be dealt with individually.  The consequences are up to the god
    dealing with the situation and may include deletion and banning.
    High level gods have been deleted and banned for abusing bugs.  If
    you *think* something may be a bug, it probably is.  

15. Players are subject to having all of their activities on this game
    monitored and recorded by mud staff members.  In the course of 
    monitoring players improperly using the game, or in the course of
    game maintenance, the activities of players may be monitored at the
    keystroke level.   Anyone playing this game expressly consents to
    such monitoring and is advised that if such monitoring reveals
    possible inappropriate activity, such evidence will be used for
    disciplinary action, which may include deletion of the player in
    question.

16. Shilling (the act of bidding on your own auctions with your multis or
    throw-away characters without the intention of actually buying the item)
    is strictly ILLEGAL and will result in a 5k fine AND the loss of the
    item.  Its illegal in real life, so don't think its not here.

17. Botting, the act of using triggers to automate tasks while away from the
    keyboard.  This is illegal and punishable if sufficient evidence exists.
    If you think someone is botting, start logging, once you are logging you
    should try to get a responce out of them by using say or tells.  If no
    response is given, save the log and inform an imm, preferably Opie or Proedus.
    Do not by any means try to deal with them yourselves, your best option is
    to log the encounter and give the log to an imm for investigation.

18. Punishments for actions stated here can be anywhere from freezer time
    to deletion.  We have final say on what punishment is given for any action
    whether or not a one is listed here.  If you don't think that the
    punishment is fair or you think that it is to harsh, too bad.  We come
    up with punishment on a case by case basis using information that might
    not always be known to you.  In other words don't stick your nose
    into something that is none of your business.

19. Rule 19 used to deal with idling while AFK. This rule is rescinded.

    These are the rules set out to date.  Just because something is 
    not here does not mean that it is not against the rules.   Use your 
    best judgement, although a select few seem to have no judgement.  
    Mudding is a privilege, NOT a right.  This game is run by a select
    few people who have the power to prevent you from returning to
    the game.  It would be highly advisable not to piss them off.
